      "title": "Experimental: Metal activity-step policy against default MlxTbccl (not a default result)",
      "summary": "Two horizontal bars, lower is better. Time per output token with the Linux host first (9/19): default MlxTbccl 14.44 ms from four lifecycles, experimental activity-step 9.48 ms from two lifecycles, a descriptive difference of minus 34 percent. The classification is insufficient evidence: two lifecycles cannot reach p of 0.05 or less in an exact test, so this is an exploratory observation, not a confirmed improvement and not a validated production optimisation. The policy costs about one busy Mac core.",
